00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:44.334
- Hello, everyone!

00:03:44.334 --> 00:03:49.030
I am from Little Rock, Arkansas,

00:03:49.030 --> 00:03:51.050
but also Memphis, Tennessee.

00:03:51.050 --> 00:03:53.090
And I grew up in the Southern Black Church

00:03:53.090 --> 00:03:56.250
and Mabel Moore is my great-grandmother.

00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:58.150
I'm gonna talk about her a little bit.

00:03:58.150 --> 00:04:01.810
And she would just
absolutely have a, I'll fit,

00:04:01.810 --> 00:04:05.377
you know, a hernia or something

00:04:05.377 --> 00:04:08.360
if she knew that I was
reading from a paper.

00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:10.480
So don't tell her, okay?
(audience laughs)

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:13.530
But some things have changed
and I've been thinking

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:18.463
a lot about recent events on
campus and just my time here.

00:04:18.463 --> 00:04:21.893
So I wrote something else
and that's why it's on paper.

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:28.150
And to me, home is essential
for centering and grounding.

00:04:28.470 --> 00:04:30.610
And I think that we have
the potential to create

00:04:30.610 --> 00:04:33.280
home in ourselves.

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:36.840
It doesn't have to be a
place, a physical place,

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:39.350
but in the interactions that
we have with one another,

00:04:39.350 --> 00:04:42.875
oftentimes Yale students
complain, it's not genuine,

00:04:42.875 --> 00:04:45.627
we ask the same questions,
we say the same things,

00:04:45.627 --> 00:04:47.883
and my goal for the year and my goal

00:04:47.883 --> 00:04:52.020
in this introduction is
just to remind us that we do

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:53.280
come from someplace.

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:56.210
Remember those things
that make you excited,

00:04:56.210 --> 00:04:58.030
that make your eyes well up,

00:04:58.030 --> 00:05:02.030
or that make you just crack up.

00:05:02.030 --> 00:05:05.300
I will be making a lot
of references about home.

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:06.550
So it's about culture,

00:05:06.550 --> 00:05:09.540
it's about mental health
and it's about faith.

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:10.930
And hopefully that comes across.

00:05:10.930 --> 00:05:13.313
Here is a bunch of little vignettes.

00:05:15.170 --> 00:05:18.640
This is for the brother
that flipped a coin

00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:21.160
that always landed on heads.

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:23.440
There was never a 50-50 chance,

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:26.200
God always knew for certain,

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:29.460
this is my busted lip and
black eye 'cause round one

00:05:29.460 --> 00:05:32.150
never ends up running around
the block up the stairs

00:05:32.150 --> 00:05:33.447
when mama is yelling,

00:05:33.447 --> 00:05:36.620
"Didn't I tell you to water my garden!"

00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:38.610
And I was just stargazing in my...

00:05:38.610 --> 00:05:41.080
And singing ritual on my
way to the gas station

00:05:41.080 --> 00:05:42.300
for a pickle.

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:44.510
Hubba Bubba and Double
Dutch, skipping rocks

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:45.520
and fishing rods.

00:05:45.520 --> 00:05:48.710
Realizing, growing up is
an obligation to my younger

00:05:48.710 --> 00:05:51.190
self to be all the beauty
I saw in butterflies

00:05:51.190 --> 00:05:54.215
breaking their backs every
time they dare to fly.

00:05:54.215 --> 00:05:55.887
This is Sarah Vaughan and
Billie Holiday laughing

00:05:55.887 --> 00:05:59.347
at dream deferred, I stole
it back and grew it up.

00:05:59.347 --> 00:06:03.543
And my naps stacked
can't touch them. (sings)

00:06:05.270 --> 00:06:06.610
Okay.

00:06:06.610 --> 00:06:09.180
When I realized I was a lamppost,

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:11.810
I was staring at the
collarbone of magnolia trees

00:06:11.810 --> 00:06:13.760
who birthed sunlight from beneath eyelids

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:15.860
that whisper sleepy dreams,

00:06:15.860 --> 00:06:18.410
celestial braids flowing down my back

00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:23.410
as my great-grandmother
greased an itchy scalp, oil,

00:06:23.550 --> 00:06:25.720
dug her fingers in the side of my arm,

00:06:25.720 --> 00:06:28.275
said you got breath
flowing like windows down

00:06:28.275 --> 00:06:30.260
on highway 365.

00:06:30.260 --> 00:06:34.490
Don't roll them up, baby.
Don't forget what you know.

00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:38.220
We face our fears at the
fulcrum of alone and awake

00:06:38.220 --> 00:06:41.240
and lucid, meet our demons on the curb.

00:06:41.240 --> 00:06:42.780
In passing.

00:06:42.780 --> 00:06:44.650
When I realized I had seen one,

00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:47.020
she had a cigarette
dangling from her lips,

00:06:47.020 --> 00:06:49.230
reaching in her bag for another.

00:06:49.230 --> 00:06:51.480
She asked me for a lighter.

00:06:51.480 --> 00:06:56.220
How easily we infatuate
ourselves and vacuums of empty.

00:06:56.220 --> 00:06:59.362
On a real, I've been sitting
in the open of my windows

00:06:59.362 --> 00:07:03.810
for days, where leaves
fold into romantic getaways

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:07.080
and the intimacy of their
brush is like the way I wish

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:09.910
our words would fold into
the corners of each other,

00:07:09.910 --> 00:07:14.910
waxing a warm sort of world,
but it all fades to black.

00:07:16.970 --> 00:07:21.120
I know how bees make
honey sweet and how seeds

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:26.120
become dandelions, field
formations for wishes come true.

00:07:26.290 --> 00:07:28.990
I know that tears fall
in the shape of rain,

00:07:28.990 --> 00:07:32.130
torrential downpours
happen inside the folds

00:07:32.130 --> 00:07:33.900
of a pillowcase.

00:07:33.900 --> 00:07:36.390
I know about sitting on
blankets on the back porch

00:07:36.390 --> 00:07:40.343
with my cousin pilling corn
husks, talking about nothing.

00:07:41.210 --> 00:07:43.503
Seems like those were the best times.

00:07:44.350 --> 00:07:47.440
I know about broken plates
and the hours it takes

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:48.610
to glue them together.

00:07:48.610 --> 00:07:50.050
I'm know people break too.

00:07:50.050 --> 00:07:53.940
I know about circles, the deep ones,

00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:56.500
that make my face into a shadow of itself,

00:07:56.500 --> 00:08:00.850
they take light with them and
make eyes into just sockets.

00:08:00.850 --> 00:08:03.500
I know about disappearing,

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:07.963
finding a mirror and talking
things back into existence.

00:08:09.520 --> 00:08:11.240
There's a ledge.

00:08:11.240 --> 00:08:13.360
And I know about letting
my feet dangle till

00:08:13.360 --> 00:08:16.443
the roaring ceases to
make my stomach boil.

00:08:17.500 --> 00:08:21.340
I know about light rooms
that feel like dark rooms

00:08:21.340 --> 00:08:25.053
and loud rooms that
feel like lonely rooms.

00:08:26.220 --> 00:08:28.380
I know in some places,

00:08:28.380 --> 00:08:32.070
the clouds seem closer to
you than they do the sky.

00:08:32.070 --> 00:08:37.070
And the sun takes up the whole
horizon. Sit here with me.

00:08:39.240 --> 00:08:43.600
We know, in some places
the cloud seem closer to us

00:08:43.600 --> 00:08:45.320
than they do the sky,

00:08:45.320 --> 00:08:48.013
and the sun takes up the whole horizon.

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:50.463
An interlude.

00:08:51.430 --> 00:08:52.360
To grow an ocean,

00:08:52.360 --> 00:08:55.690
you stick a cloud on the
tip of your tongue and blow!

00:08:55.690 --> 00:09:00.410
A prayer, a raging plea
for bursting ground,

00:09:00.410 --> 00:09:02.563
a righteous peace.

00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:07.250
I have been dreaming of
spirits that sit in the train,

00:09:07.250 --> 00:09:10.340
on a bus, in a tree, at the table.

00:09:10.340 --> 00:09:14.220
Something you walk
through that catches hands

00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:17.243
and spins merry go rounds in our sorrow.

00:09:18.090 --> 00:09:21.720
Ancestral souls whose backs
cracked open and yoked

00:09:21.720 --> 00:09:26.069
the hope holes, yolk the holes full again.

00:09:26.069 --> 00:09:31.069
I do not mean to trivialize
or beautify the ugly.

00:09:31.320 --> 00:09:34.800
I only mean to create a home,

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:38.853
a heart that bleeds seeds
of divine qualification.

00:09:39.860 --> 00:09:44.290
He who collects all my tears in a bottle,

00:09:44.290 --> 00:09:46.343
records them in a book.

00:09:47.680 --> 00:09:50.450
I didn't write that. That was in Psalms.

00:09:50.450 --> 00:09:54.750
He, who burns the book
and writes new ones,

00:09:54.750 --> 00:09:57.203
the spirit that I walk through.

00:09:58.510 --> 00:10:01.030
I do not mean to trivialize
or beautify the ugly.

00:10:01.030 --> 00:10:03.440
I only mean to create a home.

00:10:03.440 --> 00:10:07.003
A whimsical sort of freedom,
unbound and wailing.

00:10:09.024 --> 00:10:12.176
♪ All we wanna do is
break the chains off ♪

00:10:12.176 --> 00:10:15.413
♪ All we wanna do is
break the chains off ♪

00:10:15.413 --> 00:10:18.244
♪ All you wanna do is be free ♪

00:10:18.244 --> 00:10:22.390
♪ All you wanna do is be free ♪

00:10:22.390 --> 00:10:23.223
J. Cole.

00:10:24.430 --> 00:10:26.300
An interlude.

00:10:26.300 --> 00:10:28.446
The leftover bacon grease
from the pot I cooked

00:10:28.446 --> 00:10:32.140
in last night stays smeared
on the kitchen counter.

00:10:32.140 --> 00:10:36.290
I hope the ant I saw crawling
up the cabinet gets stuck.

00:10:36.290 --> 00:10:38.663
Visitors are always welcome in my home.

00:10:39.550 --> 00:10:42.950
I peel the potato and
then a cucumber and then

00:10:42.950 --> 00:10:47.510
an apple and the carrot
and some corn and then some

00:10:47.510 --> 00:10:51.870
squash and an onion, and
then a Brussel sprout,

00:10:51.870 --> 00:10:56.720
and then the beans and also a tangerine.

00:10:56.720 --> 00:11:00.910
Eat with me. I only mean to create a home.

00:11:05.011 --> 00:11:08.178
(audience applauding)

00:11:14.883 --> 00:11:17.010
- See, I told Josh she was
gonna let that light in.

00:11:17.010 --> 00:11:18.000
That was incredible.

00:11:18.000 --> 00:11:20.300
And if it feels like that
