00:14:18.540 --> 00:14:20.700
we have made a lot of strides in terms

00:14:20.700 --> 00:14:22.056
of how we talk about mental health,

00:14:22.056 --> 00:14:24.480
focusing in particular
on trying to decrease

00:14:24.480 --> 00:14:26.940
the stigma that's associated
with those conversations.

00:14:26.940 --> 00:14:29.120
But clearly there's still
a lot of room for growth

00:14:29.120 --> 00:14:31.384
in these conversations and
we still have a lot to do.

00:14:31.384 --> 00:14:32.840
And I would say that's not something

00:14:32.840 --> 00:14:34.420
that's just so unique to our campus,

00:14:34.420 --> 00:14:36.400
but it's also true nationwide.

00:14:36.400 --> 00:14:38.800
Again, where there's been lots of places

00:14:38.800 --> 00:14:40.380
where there's been improvement
in the conversation,

00:14:40.380 --> 00:14:42.280
but still room for growth and something

00:14:42.280 --> 00:14:43.602
that we're hoping to
continue to facilitate

00:14:43.602 --> 00:14:46.265
through the conversation tonight.

00:14:46.265 --> 00:14:48.420
So we're really thankful
