00:17:48.860 --> 00:17:51.830
I came here a few years
back and I'm glad to be back

00:17:51.830 --> 00:17:52.803
on the campus.

00:17:56.070 --> 00:17:57.770
Anita, that was amazing.

00:17:57.770 --> 00:18:00.460
First of all, I don't even know
where you are. There you go.

00:18:00.460 --> 00:18:03.040
Listen, I don't know if
that's what Yale produces.

00:18:03.040 --> 00:18:05.408
I need to...
(audience laughs)

00:18:05.408 --> 00:18:08.403
Find a new option for myself here.

00:18:10.610 --> 00:18:15.610
Well, I really believe that
if this is gonna be a sincere,

00:18:16.650 --> 00:18:20.423
genuine conversation, that
leaders lead in vulnerability,

00:18:20.423 --> 00:18:22.960
and in order to lead a conversation,

00:18:22.960 --> 00:18:24.050
I have to be vulnerable,

00:18:24.050 --> 00:18:26.780
which I think will generate
and promote more vulnerability.

00:18:26.780 --> 00:18:27.628
I'm sure you probably,

00:18:27.628 --> 00:18:29.920
some of you've been in
this room before or been

00:18:29.920 --> 00:18:31.900
in rooms like it, constantly.

00:18:31.900 --> 00:18:34.970
It may not be an environment
that you necessarily see

00:18:34.970 --> 00:18:38.320
as conducive for like sharing and comfort,

00:18:38.320 --> 00:18:41.010
but I just want you to imagine this place

00:18:41.010 --> 00:18:46.010
as the most comfortable
environment that you can imagine,

00:18:46.360 --> 00:18:48.820
one where we're just here
having a conversation.

00:18:48.820 --> 00:18:51.810
You're not being screened.
You're not being judged.

00:18:51.810 --> 00:18:54.270
You're not being assessed.

00:18:54.270 --> 00:18:56.280
There's no grades being
handed out at the end

00:18:56.280 --> 00:18:57.450
of this situation.

00:18:57.450 --> 00:19:01.970
This is us being free to be ourselves.

00:19:01.970 --> 00:19:03.973
And you're welcome to join in that.

00:19:03.973 --> 00:19:06.310
And I'm also just gonna allow you to,

00:19:06.310 --> 00:19:09.070
if you don't wanna join
the conversation to have

00:19:09.070 --> 00:19:12.150
a window into my soul in the process.

00:19:12.150 --> 00:19:15.913
So start a little bit about me.

00:19:17.038 --> 00:19:18.650
I'm just gonna get right into it.

00:19:18.650 --> 00:19:23.258
I, as we're talking about
this intersection of faith,

00:19:23.258 --> 00:19:26.973
mental health, social justice,

00:19:28.610 --> 00:19:30.873
I'm gonna start with the dark seasons

00:19:30.873 --> 00:19:33.291
that I've experienced in life,

00:19:33.291 --> 00:19:35.709
because I think that contributes to all

00:19:35.709 --> 00:19:37.270
of those particular issues.

00:19:37.270 --> 00:19:39.190
So for me, let me set a timer,

00:19:39.190 --> 00:19:41.460
because I can talk, all right?

00:19:41.460 --> 00:19:43.410
And we will not get
anything else accomplished

00:19:43.410 --> 00:19:44.443
in here today.

00:19:46.740 --> 00:19:51.640
But for me, I actually
recall the dark seasons

00:19:51.640 --> 00:19:54.870
of my life starting as
old as age seven, right?

00:19:54.870 --> 00:19:56.265
So seven years old,

00:19:56.265 --> 00:19:59.720
I was invited into the room
of a close family member

00:19:59.720 --> 00:20:03.530
and I was taken advantage of sexually.

00:20:03.530 --> 00:20:07.710
And so here I am seven
years old and I have to now

00:20:07.710 --> 00:20:10.510
wear these scars on the playground, right?

00:20:10.510 --> 00:20:14.220
I gotta wear these scars amongst my peers,

00:20:14.220 --> 00:20:18.750
as they are playing
four square or whatnot.

00:20:18.750 --> 00:20:21.110
I have to wear these
scars on Saturday morning

00:20:21.110 --> 00:20:22.480
when I'm watching my cartoons.

00:20:22.480 --> 00:20:26.520
I have to wear these scars of this abuse

00:20:27.820 --> 00:20:31.870
in environments with
the exact person who put

00:20:31.870 --> 00:20:35.780
these scars on me and act
as if nothing happened,

00:20:35.780 --> 00:20:37.640
because it wasn't dealt
with, it wasn't handled.

00:20:37.640 --> 00:20:40.260
So I learned something in that situation,

00:20:40.260 --> 00:20:41.470
something very unhealthy.

00:20:41.470 --> 00:20:44.710
And what I learned was to
suppress trauma and pretend

00:20:44.710 --> 00:20:46.930
as if nothing happened
and just plow through.

00:20:46.930 --> 00:20:50.050
That was the first unhealthy
lesson I learned as far

00:20:50.050 --> 00:20:54.092
as trauma was concerned was
to just, hey, box that up,

00:20:54.092 --> 00:20:55.774
keep it moving forward.

00:20:55.774 --> 00:20:57.200
If you wanna add to that,

00:20:57.200 --> 00:20:58.880
I grew up in an environment and a home

00:20:58.880 --> 00:21:00.420
that was very unhealthy.

00:21:00.420 --> 00:21:02.130
It was not a healthy environment.

00:21:02.130 --> 00:21:05.840
It was filled with immaturity. Drugs.

00:21:05.840 --> 00:21:09.870
It was filled with just
so many different nuances

00:21:09.870 --> 00:21:12.310
that made it difficult
for me to have a healthy

00:21:12.310 --> 00:21:13.743
outlook on life.

00:21:15.070 --> 00:21:17.060
Four years old, my father was gone.

00:21:17.060 --> 00:21:20.880
I never saw him again
until 25 years later.

00:21:20.880 --> 00:21:22.510
So you add to that,

00:21:22.510 --> 00:21:25.960
I was learning in that
environment of who I was

00:21:25.960 --> 00:21:28.510
supposed to be from the
models in my community.

00:21:28.510 --> 00:21:32.020
And so what that led to
is a young man who had

00:21:32.020 --> 00:21:34.920
experienced everything,

00:21:34.920 --> 00:21:38.653
from physical abuse, drugs,

00:21:40.061 --> 00:21:42.110
as I said before, sexual abuse.

00:21:42.110 --> 00:21:45.240
And now I was not just the
recipient of these things.

00:21:45.240 --> 00:21:47.370
I was starting to take
on these characteristics

00:21:47.370 --> 00:21:49.790
and flesh them out on a day-to-day basis

00:21:49.790 --> 00:21:52.470
to where the police were coming
to my house consistently.

00:21:52.470 --> 00:21:56.320
I found myself consistently
depressed and in a messed

00:21:56.320 --> 00:21:59.773
up state of being, this is
all before the age of 18.

00:22:01.510 --> 00:22:04.890
But I remember as a kid, people saying,

00:22:04.890 --> 00:22:06.180
you remind me of your father.

00:22:06.180 --> 00:22:07.980
You act like your father.
You're just like your father.

00:22:07.980 --> 00:22:09.392
You're similar to your father.

00:22:09.392 --> 00:22:13.653
And I didn't take it as a compliment,

00:22:15.540 --> 00:22:17.230
even if it was just a mere observation.

00:22:17.230 --> 00:22:18.670
I took it as an insult,

00:22:18.670 --> 00:22:21.060
because this was a man
that wasn't consistent.

00:22:21.060 --> 00:22:23.139
This was a man that had
taken on drug abuse.

00:22:23.139 --> 00:22:27.830
And probably has a lot of
mental health issues himself.

00:22:27.830 --> 00:22:31.357
But I saw that as an example
of who I should not be.

00:22:31.357 --> 00:22:33.470
And so what I did at
that point in time was

00:22:33.470 --> 00:22:38.250
consumed myself with not being my father.

00:22:38.250 --> 00:22:40.170
I didn't consume myself with figuring

00:22:40.170 --> 00:22:41.610
out who I was supposed to be.

00:22:41.610 --> 00:22:45.430
I consumed myself with not
being this example of a person.

00:22:45.430 --> 00:22:47.270
So I took that initiative.

00:22:47.270 --> 00:22:51.140
But the problem in me trying
so hard to not be him was

00:22:51.140 --> 00:22:52.790
I didn't know who I was supposed to be.

00:22:52.790 --> 00:22:54.050
And on top of that,

00:22:54.050 --> 00:22:56.010
all the trauma that I had experienced

00:22:56.010 --> 00:22:57.570
throughout this period of time,

00:22:57.570 --> 00:23:02.570
I was just stuffing it a way,
all the pain, all the abuse,

00:23:02.960 --> 00:23:04.020
all of those particular things.

00:23:04.020 --> 00:23:06.080
I was stuffing it away because
I had an agenda and I had

00:23:06.080 --> 00:23:08.810
a mission and that was
to not be my father.

00:23:08.810 --> 00:23:12.600
And so, externally, I
was succeeding, right?

00:23:12.600 --> 00:23:15.310
Externally I'm succeeding.
I got scholarships.

00:23:15.310 --> 00:23:17.190
I went to college, I made the Dean's list.

00:23:17.190 --> 00:23:20.181
I graduated, I interned, I
got a good corporate job,

00:23:20.181 --> 00:23:22.390
after corporate job I started a business,

00:23:22.390 --> 00:23:24.010
a successful business at that,

00:23:24.010 --> 00:23:27.623
but internally I was headed for disaster.

00:23:28.740 --> 00:23:30.360
So externally I'm succeeding,

00:23:30.360 --> 00:23:33.670
but internally I'm failing tremendously,

00:23:33.670 --> 00:23:35.123
but I don't even realize it.

00:23:36.643 --> 00:23:39.150
I learned to take the
worst circumstances of life

00:23:39.150 --> 00:23:41.370
and push them deep down
into this internal closet.

00:23:41.370 --> 00:23:44.592
And I'm bleeding internally,
but I'm thinking I'm okay.

00:23:44.592 --> 00:23:49.070
And if you have a vital
wound and you ignore it,

00:23:49.070 --> 00:23:50.820
it doesn't get better.

00:23:50.820 --> 00:23:52.123
It eventually kills you.

00:23:53.710 --> 00:23:55.110
So I'm moving a million miles an hour.

00:23:55.110 --> 00:23:56.520
Now there's a marriage.
There's three kids.

00:23:56.520 --> 00:23:57.590
It's running multiple businesses.

00:23:57.590 --> 00:24:00.240
The successful music
career. I'm winning Grammys.

00:24:00.240 --> 00:24:02.137
New York times bestselling author.

00:24:02.137 --> 00:24:04.100
And then it all came to a head.

00:24:07.049 --> 00:24:07.882
In front of the world I was

00:24:07.882 --> 00:24:09.000
just level-headed God-fearing man.

00:24:09.000 --> 00:24:11.610
I'm navigating everything
just the way that I should.

00:24:11.610 --> 00:24:14.610
But behind the scenes,
I'm a ticking time bomb,

00:24:14.610 --> 00:24:17.410
ignoring all of the trauma,

00:24:17.410 --> 00:24:21.160
ignoring all of the weight
of these experiences

00:24:21.160 --> 00:24:24.455
and this depression that is
knocking at my front door.

00:24:24.455 --> 00:24:25.780
And it was during this time,

00:24:25.780 --> 00:24:28.190
I remember watching a
video of a young man,

00:24:28.190 --> 00:24:30.551
probably about 15 years old
in Chicago, and he's waving

00:24:30.551 --> 00:24:33.220
a gun around and flaunting it.

00:24:33.220 --> 00:24:36.640
And I remember something
being triggered, right?

00:24:36.640 --> 00:24:37.930
It moved me almost to tears.

00:24:37.930 --> 00:24:40.001
I learned about the facts of
the murder rate in Chicago.

00:24:40.001 --> 00:24:42.480
And I was, and I found myself sitting

00:24:42.480 --> 00:24:44.850
there emotionally just devastated.

00:24:44.850 --> 00:24:45.980
And I couldn't understand why.

00:24:45.980 --> 00:24:49.230
Well, truthfully, I had
a friend who was taken

00:24:49.230 --> 00:24:50.990
by gun violence at age 13 years old,

00:24:50.990 --> 00:24:52.100
and that trauma was triggered.

00:24:52.100 --> 00:24:53.403
I didn't even realize it.

00:24:55.430 --> 00:24:59.010
I was the victim of this,

00:24:59.010 --> 00:25:02.680
witnessing a death of a teenager.

00:25:02.680 --> 00:25:04.401
And then I'm seeing this
other teenager just flaunting.

00:25:04.401 --> 00:25:07.250
And I didn't even connect those dots.

00:25:07.250 --> 00:25:10.210
Later that year, I remember
hearing about the death

00:25:10.210 --> 00:25:11.110
of Trayvon Martin.

00:25:13.165 --> 00:25:17.510
Now, I was affected, right?
I'm affected by this murder.

00:25:17.510 --> 00:25:18.470
I'm affected by what's happened

00:25:18.470 --> 00:25:21.330
to Trayvon, but I didn't
know how to express it.

00:25:21.330 --> 00:25:24.517
I didn't know what avenues or
venues I had to express it.

00:25:24.517 --> 00:25:25.670
And so once again,

00:25:25.670 --> 00:25:28.180
the same thing I had learned
previously to take trauma,

00:25:28.180 --> 00:25:30.380
to take traumatizing
experiences and stuff them

00:25:30.380 --> 00:25:33.120
away is what I practiced.

00:25:33.120 --> 00:25:36.290
So I'm disturbed to the
core. I'm fueled with anger.

00:25:36.290 --> 00:25:37.790
I remember as a kid

00:25:37.790 --> 00:25:40.640
seeing my mother fueled
with anger and frustration

00:25:40.640 --> 00:25:42.930
after Rodney King was
beaten down and her hearing

00:25:42.930 --> 00:25:45.350
the verdict and all these
particular things happened,

00:25:45.350 --> 00:25:46.940
but I don't know how to navigate

00:25:46.940 --> 00:25:48.190
this particular circumstance.

00:25:48.190 --> 00:25:52.610
And so I'm sitting in a
similar position in a couple

00:25:52.610 --> 00:25:54.130
of years after Trayvon, it was

00:25:54.130 --> 00:25:56.280
Renisha McBride, a young teenager who got

00:25:56.280 --> 00:25:57.925
in a car accident and
knocked on someone's door

00:25:57.925 --> 00:26:01.691
and was killed because she
was profiled and thought

00:26:01.691 --> 00:26:04.223
to be committing a crime.

00:26:05.090 --> 00:26:07.560
After Renisha McBride, there was

00:26:07.560 --> 00:26:09.420
Eric Garner and after
Eric Garner, there was

00:26:09.420 --> 00:26:12.000
Michael Brown and so
on and so on and Sandra

00:26:12.000 --> 00:26:13.960
and so on and so on and so on and so on,

00:26:13.960 --> 00:26:18.960
and then, and then, and
then there were riots.

00:26:21.770 --> 00:26:23.560
And I found myself sitting
in the middle of all

00:26:23.560 --> 00:26:25.433
this wondering where do I fit?

00:26:25.433 --> 00:26:28.263
I how do I react?

00:26:29.650 --> 00:26:32.470
I was trying to hide away
the trauma of seeing people,

00:26:32.470 --> 00:26:34.330
who may as well have been
my cousins, my sisters,

00:26:34.330 --> 00:26:38.840
my nieces, my aunts, being
killed, but it was overwhelming.

00:26:38.840 --> 00:26:40.739
And I found myself in the
streets of Atlanta involved

00:26:40.739 --> 00:26:42.690
in a protest.

00:26:42.690 --> 00:26:44.340
So here I am protesting in this,

00:26:44.340 --> 00:26:47.210
students from all the
surrounding colleges in the area

00:26:47.210 --> 00:26:48.197
are protesting with me.

00:26:48.197 --> 00:26:50.700
And all of them are
looking to me for guidance,

00:26:50.700 --> 00:26:51.792
for wisdom, for leadership.

00:26:51.792 --> 00:26:53.993
And I'm just as lost as they are.

00:26:55.067 --> 00:26:57.690
I have no idea how to navigate everything

00:26:57.690 --> 00:26:58.523
that I'm dealing with.

00:26:58.523 --> 00:27:00.600
And at the same time, I'm this respected,

00:27:00.600 --> 00:27:02.700
seemingly conservative artist.

00:27:02.700 --> 00:27:04.239
And a lot of my supporters
didn't like the idea

00:27:04.239 --> 00:27:06.360
of me getting involved in what to them was

00:27:06.360 --> 00:27:07.593
a political affair.

00:27:08.650 --> 00:27:10.040
What are you doing getting involved

00:27:10.040 --> 00:27:12.210
in this political affair?

00:27:12.210 --> 00:27:16.270
And so the dilemma that I had was dual.

00:27:16.270 --> 00:27:19.370
It was me trying to get
involved and do something

00:27:19.370 --> 00:27:20.680
about things that I'm seeing happening.

00:27:20.680 --> 00:27:21.513
But then also,

00:27:21.513 --> 00:27:25.050
I don't even know who I
am in the middle of this.

00:27:25.050 --> 00:27:26.927
So I'm trying to find myself.
I don't know who I wanna be.

00:27:26.927 --> 00:27:29.930
And my identity had already been forged

00:27:29.930 --> 00:27:32.123
by finding approval in other people.

00:27:33.230 --> 00:27:34.160
So I was losing,

00:27:34.160 --> 00:27:37.170
my approval rate was going
down in one particular group,

00:27:37.170 --> 00:27:39.633
as I'm trying to do
what I felt to be right.

00:27:40.720 --> 00:27:42.020
And the trauma's weighing.

00:27:44.230 --> 00:27:46.480
I felt what Moses, if you know anything

00:27:46.480 --> 00:27:51.480
about Moses, Moses was Hebrew by birth,

00:27:51.530 --> 00:27:54.550
but he was adopted by
the Egyptian aristocracy.

00:27:54.550 --> 00:27:58.770
And it came upon him one day,
oh my goodness, I am Hebrew.

00:27:58.770 --> 00:28:00.370
And the Hebrew people are being oppressed

00:28:00.370 --> 00:28:02.620
by the Egyptians, but yet I'm a part

00:28:02.620 --> 00:28:04.110
of this Egypt aristocracy.

00:28:04.110 --> 00:28:07.233
How does this make sense? What do I do?

00:28:08.149 --> 00:28:09.860
And so I took a page out of Moses's book,

00:28:09.860 --> 00:28:12.830
you know what Moses did
was he killed somebody.

00:28:12.830 --> 00:28:14.015
That's not what I did.

00:28:14.015 --> 00:28:17.010
(audience laughs)

00:28:17.010 --> 00:28:18.423
I tweeted.

00:28:18.423 --> 00:28:20.733
(audience laughs)
Same-same.

00:28:22.670 --> 00:28:25.140
I tweeted a lot, right? I'm tweeting.

00:28:25.140 --> 00:28:27.100
But I'm saying things
outside of the boundaries

00:28:27.100 --> 00:28:28.230
of what people expected of me,

00:28:28.230 --> 00:28:30.070
I'm on national television after this,

00:28:30.070 --> 00:28:32.180
I'm writing articles
after this, I'm on CNN.

00:28:32.180 --> 00:28:36.687
And the result was this
unadulterated rejection.

00:28:41.210 --> 00:28:43.130
So I'm despised now. I'm hated.

00:28:43.130 --> 00:28:44.580
I've lost support regularly.

00:28:44.580 --> 00:28:47.250
And I was about to learn
a very beautiful lesson

00:28:47.250 --> 00:28:48.500
that stays with me to this day.

00:28:48.500 --> 00:28:50.880
And that lesson was, if you
live for people's acceptance,

00:28:50.880 --> 00:28:52.933
you will die from their rejection.

00:28:58.400 --> 00:28:59.540
So I stood for something,

00:28:59.540 --> 00:29:01.163
but it felt like I lost everything.

00:29:02.180 --> 00:29:03.920
I worked so hard to not be
my father, to be respected,

00:29:03.920 --> 00:29:06.950
to be successful, to be
accomplished, to be accepted,

00:29:06.950 --> 00:29:07.890
and now I'm hated.

00:29:07.890 --> 00:29:10.370
I mean, in days, days, y'all,

00:29:10.370 --> 00:29:13.500
I lost hundreds of thousands
of social media followers.

00:29:13.500 --> 00:29:16.503
It'd drive a 15 year old crazy, right?

00:29:16.503 --> 00:29:18.757
(audience laughs)

00:29:18.757 --> 00:29:21.049
I was bombarded with
messages of people telling me

00:29:21.049 --> 00:29:23.410
how much respect they lost for me.

00:29:23.410 --> 00:29:26.333
I was bombarded with hateful messages.

00:29:26.333 --> 00:29:30.700
People sent me videos of
them burning my music,

00:29:30.700 --> 00:29:32.058
like with fire.

00:29:32.058 --> 00:29:34.073
(audience laughs)

00:29:34.073 --> 00:29:35.959
At least they bought it though.

00:29:35.959 --> 00:29:38.792
(audience laughs)

00:29:39.630 --> 00:29:41.680
See the bright side in everything, right?

00:29:44.730 --> 00:29:49.513
I couldn't understand how
they didn't hear my pain,

00:29:50.370 --> 00:29:53.980
how my sorrow and my pain
that I was already taught

00:29:53.980 --> 00:29:56.140
to suppress, and now
here I was expressing was

00:29:56.140 --> 00:29:58.040
being pushed away.

00:29:58.040 --> 00:30:00.853
It created a mental chaos for me.

00:30:02.200 --> 00:30:03.650
I mean, some of it's to be expected.

00:30:03.650 --> 00:30:06.610
We don't always wanna hear
the voices of people speak

00:30:06.610 --> 00:30:08.978
on social or political things.

00:30:08.978 --> 00:30:10.970
"LeBron James, stop talking

00:30:10.970 --> 00:30:12.470
about this and just play basketball.

00:30:12.470 --> 00:30:14.170
We don't wanna hear that from you.

00:30:15.050 --> 00:30:17.430
We don't wanna hear the
nuance of who you are."

00:30:17.430 --> 00:30:21.980
But still, I was at this crossroads,

00:30:21.980 --> 00:30:24.130
this downward spiral started
to happen in my life.

00:30:24.130 --> 00:30:25.360
And at the lowest point,

00:30:25.360 --> 00:30:29.130
I started to get hate
messages and death threats

00:30:29.130 --> 00:30:30.440
on myself and my family.

00:30:30.440 --> 00:30:32.930
Racial slurs consistently pouring in,

00:30:32.930 --> 00:30:37.930
and I was spiraling downward,
anger, depression, sadness,

00:30:39.700 --> 00:30:43.023
frustration, a feeling of being trapped.

00:30:45.000 --> 00:30:48.210
And I didn't know what was
real. I lost faith in people.

00:30:48.210 --> 00:30:51.803
I lost faith in God.
I lost faith in faith.

00:30:53.410 --> 00:30:56.020
So maybe that's not your story.

00:30:56.020 --> 00:30:58.120
That's not why you're in this room, right?

00:30:59.330 --> 00:31:04.330
Maybe that's not how you
came to a place of emotional,

00:31:04.930 --> 00:31:08.270
spiritual or mental chaos.

00:31:08.270 --> 00:31:12.520
But you do know what it feels like to have

00:31:12.520 --> 00:31:14.720
the world sitting on your
shoulders and you feel

00:31:14.720 --> 00:31:17.360
so lonely you wanna quit.

00:31:17.360 --> 00:31:19.300
You do know what it
feels like to feel like

00:31:19.300 --> 00:31:20.280
everyone's depending

00:31:20.280 --> 00:31:22.510
on you and this pressure is overwhelming.

00:31:22.510 --> 00:31:25.040
You do know what it feels
like for people to expect

00:31:25.040 --> 00:31:29.463
your best, but you're
really at your worst.

00:31:30.390 --> 00:31:34.250
But how do we navigate that?
How do we navigate that chaos?

00:31:34.250 --> 00:31:36.940
And how do we continue
dreaming and creating?

00:31:36.940 --> 00:31:38.860
I know I wish I could tell
you I just woke up one day

00:31:38.860 --> 00:31:39.750
and I just found some courage.

00:31:39.750 --> 00:31:42.170
And I just said, you
know what? I don't care.

00:31:42.170 --> 00:31:43.460
I wish I could tell you that's the case.

00:31:43.460 --> 00:31:46.660
I wish I could tell you I
just look deep inside myself

00:31:46.660 --> 00:31:49.400
and I found something and pushed through.

00:31:49.400 --> 00:31:50.650
That's not what happened.

00:31:51.680 --> 00:31:54.870
What happened to me was
I had to open the closet.

00:31:54.870 --> 00:31:59.060
I had to look in that closet
that I had stuffed away,

00:31:59.060 --> 00:32:01.490
all of that trauma, all of that pain,

00:32:01.490 --> 00:32:03.200
all of that suffering.

00:32:03.200 --> 00:32:07.000
And I had to stare it in the
face. All of that failure.

00:32:07.000 --> 00:32:09.650
I had to stare it in the face.

00:32:09.650 --> 00:32:12.820
I had to look at it and allow it

00:32:12.820 --> 00:32:15.863
to make me a new me.

00:32:17.470 --> 00:32:19.553
I had to embrace the trauma
and allow it to mold me

00:32:19.553 --> 00:32:20.390
into something new.

00:32:20.390 --> 00:32:22.529
See, the shift is being
willing to die to whatever

00:32:22.529 --> 00:32:26.730
it was that we were
before the pain to birth

00:32:26.730 --> 00:32:28.463
the person that we're becoming.

00:32:29.660 --> 00:32:32.420
Right, the shift is
sometimes we're too attached

00:32:32.420 --> 00:32:36.033
to who we've been so we're
held back to who we can become.

00:32:37.370 --> 00:32:41.440
We don't understand that there
is no triumph without trial.

00:32:41.440 --> 00:32:43.530
We don't understand, like
working out in the gym,

00:32:43.530 --> 00:32:45.893
you've got to fail in
order to get stronger.

00:32:47.670 --> 00:32:49.750
It's like a foreign concept.

00:32:49.750 --> 00:32:51.670
So I had to be willing to work and walk

00:32:51.670 --> 00:32:53.680
through judgment and
inconvenience in order to grow,

00:32:53.680 --> 00:32:56.860
I had to be willing to become
who I was created to be,

00:32:56.860 --> 00:32:58.763
not who they wanted me to be.

00:33:00.980 --> 00:33:02.130
So it's scary, right?

00:33:02.130 --> 00:33:03.590
It's, you're standing at
the edge of something new,

00:33:03.590 --> 00:33:04.960
you're afraid to jump and you're,

00:33:04.960 --> 00:33:07.669
you don't know what that's
gonna, what the cost,

00:33:07.669 --> 00:33:10.710
the opportunity cost, the cost analysis

00:33:10.710 --> 00:33:11.543
of that situation is.

00:33:11.543 --> 00:33:12.470
And so you're scared to jump.

00:33:12.470 --> 00:33:14.570
I know what exactly what
it is to be scared to jump.

00:33:14.570 --> 00:33:18.290
I was in New Zealand and I'm on

00:33:21.654 --> 00:33:23.233
this 700 foot tower.

00:33:24.100 --> 00:33:25.543
And they say, come on, man,
we got jump off this thing,

00:33:25.543 --> 00:33:27.810
it's a base jump, it'll be fun.

00:33:27.810 --> 00:33:29.280
And I was like, I don't know
if you check my skin tone any,

00:33:29.280 --> 00:33:32.213
but this is kind of something
black people don't do.

00:33:32.213 --> 00:33:35.340
(audience laughs)

00:33:35.340 --> 00:33:37.100
But they convinced me, man, it'll be fun.

00:33:37.100 --> 00:33:37.933
We should do it.

00:33:37.933 --> 00:33:40.421
They show me a video of
Beyonce jumping off of it.

00:33:40.421 --> 00:33:43.470
(audience laughs)

00:33:43.470 --> 00:33:46.010
But see, there's a million
things Beyonce can do

00:33:46.010 --> 00:33:48.360
that I can't so that's
not really a good...

00:33:49.990 --> 00:33:53.393
So I get up there and I'm
telling myself, let's do it.

00:33:54.320 --> 00:33:56.960
And I look down and I see
Tupac and Michael Jackson

00:33:56.960 --> 00:33:57.985
waving at me.

00:33:57.985 --> 00:34:00.860
(audience laughs)

00:34:00.860 --> 00:34:02.870
And I say, I'm not gonna be able to jump.

00:34:02.870 --> 00:34:04.227
I can't do this.

00:34:04.227 --> 00:34:05.190
And they said, fine,

00:34:05.190 --> 00:34:07.855
can you move out the way so
this 11 year old girl can jump?

00:34:07.855 --> 00:34:09.570
(audience laughs)

00:34:09.570 --> 00:34:13.850
So then I had to jump. But
I'm better because of it.

00:34:13.850 --> 00:34:15.970
I wouldn't even be able
to tell you the story had

00:34:15.970 --> 00:34:17.160
I not taken that jump.

00:34:17.160 --> 00:34:19.180
We're so afraid to jump
because we're so focused

00:34:19.180 --> 00:34:21.800
on how far the fall is.

00:34:21.800 --> 00:34:23.480
We're so focused on what the failure

00:34:23.480 --> 00:34:24.930
of that jump looks like.

00:34:24.930 --> 00:34:28.091
And we have to become something new.

00:34:28.091 --> 00:34:30.720
We have to take our traumas
and allow them to make us

00:34:30.720 --> 00:34:31.850
a part of who we wanna be.

00:34:31.850 --> 00:34:34.780
Take the terrible events
and create a story

00:34:34.780 --> 00:34:36.440
of triumph, right?

00:34:36.440 --> 00:34:39.030
Athletes don't quit at the
toughest part of the game,

00:34:39.030 --> 00:34:43.400
that's when they wanna
play harder, dream higher,

00:34:43.400 --> 00:34:47.300
push further, become something new.

00:34:47.300 --> 00:34:49.875
You don't despise the caterpillar.

00:34:49.875 --> 00:34:51.790
You don't despise the cocoon that turns

00:34:51.790 --> 00:34:53.200
a caterpillar into a butterfly, right?

00:34:53.200 --> 00:34:54.300
It doesn't make sense.

00:34:54.300 --> 00:34:58.970
And so sometimes recognizing
and realizing, you know what?

00:34:58.970 --> 00:35:01.150
I'm broken and there's
some issues in my life

00:35:01.150 --> 00:35:04.500
that I need to address, I need
to face, I need to look at,

00:35:04.500 --> 00:35:05.900
I need to talk about,

00:35:05.900 --> 00:35:08.690
is the only way to get to
the other side of them.

00:35:08.690 --> 00:35:10.100
And had I not addressed them,

00:35:10.100 --> 00:35:11.580
had I not looked in the closet,

00:35:11.580 --> 00:35:14.480
had I not stared in the face
of these particular things?

00:35:14.480 --> 00:35:16.370
I wouldn't have seen what
I believe God was trying

00:35:16.370 --> 00:35:21.370
to do was make me into a
better version of myself,

00:35:21.630 --> 00:35:24.240
was build me into something else.

00:35:24.240 --> 00:35:25.390
And so I own my story.

00:35:25.390 --> 00:35:27.610
And that's what we've gotta,
we've gotta own our story.

00:35:27.610 --> 00:35:30.210
I had to own my story and
say, this is who I am,

00:35:30.210 --> 00:35:32.090
this is what made me who I am,

00:35:32.090 --> 00:35:34.627
this is a part of my
journey and because of that,

00:35:34.627 --> 00:35:37.250
I am who I am.

00:35:37.250 --> 00:35:38.300
The strength that I have

00:35:38.300 --> 00:35:42.201
is because of what I've gone through.

00:35:42.201 --> 00:35:43.920
These are our scars, right?

00:35:43.920 --> 00:35:47.730
We show people our scars to
prove that healing is real.

00:35:47.730 --> 00:35:48.646
If no one shows you their scars,

00:35:48.646 --> 00:35:50.432
you walk around believing like, oh,

00:35:50.432 --> 00:35:53.030
there's no coming back from that.

00:35:53.030 --> 00:35:55.290
But then here are real
life people saying, no,

00:35:55.290 --> 00:35:57.130
I have these same scars,

00:35:57.130 --> 00:36:00.273
I survived and I'm
stronger and so are you,

00:36:01.250 --> 00:36:03.743
but first you've gotta
admit that you're wounded.

00:36:06.620 --> 00:36:08.843
I could tell a million stories.

00:36:10.680 --> 00:36:12.973
One story that comes to mind is Raison.

00:36:14.110 --> 00:36:17.320
Raison Harris, who is incarcerated

00:36:17.320 --> 00:36:20.110
at San Quentin and Raison was incarcerated

00:36:20.110 --> 00:36:24.950
because he took a man's
life and he's doing 55

00:36:24.950 --> 00:36:25.950
years to life.

00:36:25.950 --> 00:36:28.190
When he went into prison, he
was depressed. He was angry.

00:36:28.190 --> 00:36:29.023
He was bitter.

00:36:29.023 --> 00:36:30.320
He was frustrated because
he made a decision

00:36:30.320 --> 00:36:33.890
as a youngster that is now
affected the rest of his life.

00:36:33.890 --> 00:36:35.650
But after a few years,
he said, you know what?

00:36:35.650 --> 00:36:39.230
I'm not going to allow
this circumstance to change

00:36:39.230 --> 00:36:40.540
my outlook on life.

00:36:40.540 --> 00:36:43.220
I'm going to use this
time to become a better

00:36:43.220 --> 00:36:44.830
version of myself.

00:36:44.830 --> 00:36:46.870
So he took financial literacy classes.

00:36:46.870 --> 00:36:48.100
He took writing classes.

00:36:48.100 --> 00:36:49.720
He became a writer

00:36:49.720 --> 00:36:51.518
for the San Quentin
Newspaper, which is the only

00:36:51.518 --> 00:36:55.453
inmate operated and run
newspaper in existence,

00:36:55.453 --> 00:37:00.330
his writings and his stories
now appear in Vice, in GQ.

00:37:00.330 --> 00:37:05.330
And if the Board and the
Governor and God are on his side,

00:37:06.120 --> 00:37:10.740
which I believe they are, he's
going to walk out, paroled,

00:37:10.740 --> 00:37:14.623
with a career in journalism
and stock investments

00:37:14.623 --> 00:37:18.810
from all the years he was
investing while he was locked up.

00:37:18.810 --> 00:37:21.460
And so had he sat in it and just said, oh,

00:37:21.460 --> 00:37:23.280
this is my fate in life,

00:37:23.280 --> 00:37:24.770
it would have been a terrible situation,

00:37:24.770 --> 00:37:25.840
but because he said, you know what,

00:37:25.840 --> 00:37:27.320
I'm gonna let this mold
me into something new,

00:37:27.320 --> 00:37:29.270
I'm gonna own this, I'm gonna admit this,

00:37:29.270 --> 00:37:32.540
I'm in a bad state and
I'm gonna acknowledge

00:37:32.540 --> 00:37:33.540
it and figure out how I can work

00:37:33.540 --> 00:37:36.980
through this is the only way
to come out on the other side.

00:37:36.980 --> 00:37:41.980
And so I'll say this. That's
where my plane landed.

00:37:41.980 --> 00:37:45.340
My plane landed with me
acknowledging I'm broken,

00:37:45.340 --> 00:37:47.200
acknowledging I'm not perfect,

00:37:47.200 --> 00:37:48.850
acknowledging I don't get it all right,

00:37:48.850 --> 00:37:52.570
acknowledging I have a
lot of wounds that are now

00:37:52.570 --> 00:37:53.687
healed and have become scars.

00:37:53.687 --> 00:37:56.040
And I can stand here today
and show you my scars,

00:37:56.040 --> 00:37:58.642
because those wounds have healed.

00:37:58.642 --> 00:38:01.182
But you've gotta admit it, right?

00:38:01.182 --> 00:38:05.370
And so that has restored
my faith in faith.

00:38:05.370 --> 00:38:06.630
That has restored my faith

00:38:06.630 --> 00:38:08.590
in God, because God is
the healer of all things

00:38:08.590 --> 00:38:10.663
and my wounds are healed because of him.

00:38:12.270 --> 00:38:17.270
And I was fighting so hard
to not be my father, right?

00:38:17.440 --> 00:38:19.180
I'm fighting so hard to not be my father,

00:38:19.180 --> 00:38:22.373
I didn't realize who I was supposed to be.

00:38:23.510 --> 00:38:26.670
So a I'm at track meet for my son.

00:38:26.670 --> 00:38:27.930
My oldest son is 10 years old.

00:38:27.930 --> 00:38:30.913
He's running track and track
meets are extremely boring.

00:38:32.330 --> 00:38:33.963
They're long and hot.

00:38:34.970 --> 00:38:36.670
His first has been at eight in the morning

00:38:36.670 --> 00:38:37.570
