00:38:37.570 --> 00:38:39.490
they don't even tell you
when it is and it's at three.

00:38:39.490 --> 00:38:42.583
So you just sit in there,
like, when is it gonna come in?

00:38:43.566 --> 00:38:44.527
And I'm there were my five-year-old

00:38:44.527 --> 00:38:47.300
and my five-year-old is
bored out of his mind.

00:38:47.300 --> 00:38:48.690
So I'm trying to keep his attention.

00:38:48.690 --> 00:38:52.537
And I say, hey, what do you
wanna do with your life?

00:38:52.537 --> 00:38:55.282
(audience laughs)

00:38:55.282 --> 00:38:56.330
I thought that was appropriate.

00:38:56.330 --> 00:39:00.130
I was trying. I mean,
he's struggling, right?

00:39:00.130 --> 00:39:03.810
Like he's struggling,
like ah, ah, the weight

00:39:03.810 --> 00:39:05.140
of the world on his
five-year-old shoulders.

00:39:05.140 --> 00:39:07.354
And he says, "Daddy, I don't know,

00:39:07.354 --> 00:39:09.137
I just wanna be like you."

00:39:11.550 --> 00:39:16.190
And listen, I would not be
the me he wants to be like,

00:39:16.190 --> 00:39:21.187
had I not owned my past

00:39:22.130 --> 00:39:24.100
and present circumstances,

00:39:24.100 --> 00:39:26.830
failures, situations and
allowed it to mold me

00:39:26.830 --> 00:39:29.080
into the me that I am today.

00:39:29.080 --> 00:39:32.130
There wouldn't be a me
he aspires to be had

00:39:32.130 --> 00:39:34.160
I not owned that.

00:39:34.160 --> 00:39:36.660
So I say to you all,

00:39:36.660 --> 00:39:40.080
I'm grateful for the
opportunity to show my scars,

00:39:40.080 --> 00:39:43.730
to admit my brokenness and
to allow that to continue

00:39:43.730 --> 00:39:46.179
to make me into a better
version of myself.

00:39:46.179 --> 00:39:47.162
Thank you.

00:39:47.162 --> 00:39:50.329
