00:44:38.366 --> 00:44:40.984
Again, the biggest thing that I want

00:44:40.984 --> 00:44:45.984
to acknowledge is that you
have to recognize you need

00:44:46.150 --> 00:44:47.923
a healthy mental state, right?

00:44:49.180 --> 00:44:52.890
And if you think you can
just plow through life

00:44:52.890 --> 00:44:55.300
without investigating,
it's like driving a car

00:44:55.300 --> 00:44:59.080
and never looking under the
hood or getting it checked out,

00:44:59.080 --> 00:45:02.810
or just thinking everything
will be fine for life.

00:45:02.810 --> 00:45:04.060
And I'm sure there's some people who do

00:45:04.060 --> 00:45:06.363
that now, not smart.

00:45:07.860 --> 00:45:10.450
So that was the biggest thing for me was

00:45:10.450 --> 00:45:12.680
to acknowledge that

00:45:14.380 --> 00:45:16.850
even if I feel like I'm able

00:45:16.850 --> 00:45:18.740
to accomplish the things
that I'm able to do

00:45:18.740 --> 00:45:22.590
on a regular basis, maybe
I'm not healthy here.

00:45:22.590 --> 00:45:26.430
And so it's been going to
see counselors or therapy.

00:45:26.430 --> 00:45:27.263
And to me,

00:45:27.263 --> 00:45:30.130
counselors is going to get
a checkup on my car, right?

00:45:30.130 --> 00:45:31.498
It's like going to the, just the physical,

00:45:31.498 --> 00:45:33.300
it's taking care of myself.

00:45:33.300 --> 00:45:36.600
So that was step one, I think, for me,

00:45:36.600 --> 00:45:38.412
and then the continual practice,

00:45:38.412 --> 00:45:43.412
is now I have language or
playing field to understand,

00:45:46.400 --> 00:45:51.400
because I'm talking to
someone who is trained

00:45:52.240 --> 00:45:53.200
in this particular area.

00:45:53.200 --> 00:45:56.813
So now I have language and
practice to do some self care.

00:45:57.760 --> 00:46:00.612
And self care for me, I was
talking about this earlier,

00:46:00.612 --> 00:46:05.040
is understanding that I need time

00:46:05.040 --> 00:46:07.500
to not be busy.

00:46:07.500 --> 00:46:11.250
I think busyness, in many ways means,

00:46:11.250 --> 00:46:13.600
your life is out of control.

00:46:13.600 --> 00:46:15.510
You don't have control over
it 'cause you're so busy.

00:46:15.510 --> 00:46:16.550
So I need time.

00:46:16.550 --> 00:46:19.410
I say I do DWA, that's a daily diversion,

00:46:19.410 --> 00:46:22.230
a weekly withdrawal,
and an annual abandon.

00:46:22.230 --> 00:46:25.403
And so daily diversion is
just, even if it's an hour,

00:46:26.240 --> 00:46:28.780
just daily, where I can, if
I use my mind all the time,

00:46:28.780 --> 00:46:29.613
let me use my hands,

00:46:29.613 --> 00:46:32.153
let me go play with Play-Doh
or color or do something.

00:46:32.153 --> 00:46:32.986
You know what I mean?

00:46:32.986 --> 00:46:36.340
With my, to where I'm just
diverted from all the things

00:46:36.340 --> 00:46:37.570
I have going on.

00:46:37.570 --> 00:46:40.320
A weekly withdrawal is just
taking a day weekly and saying,

00:46:40.320 --> 00:46:42.000
I'm gonna stop.

00:46:42.000 --> 00:46:42.833
I'm gonna pause.

00:46:42.833 --> 00:46:44.470
I'm gonna do something
that has nothing to do

00:46:44.470 --> 00:46:47.270
with the things that are stressing me out.

00:46:47.270 --> 00:46:49.300
And then an annual abandon
is just taking some

00:46:49.300 --> 00:46:52.320
time every year to get away from it all.

00:46:52.320 --> 00:46:56.590
And that's, that's me,
you know what I mean?

00:46:56.590 --> 00:46:59.700
So that's not necessarily the
prescription for everyone,

00:46:59.700 --> 00:47:01.250
because everyone has
different issues going on,

00:47:01.250 --> 00:47:03.533
but that's how I'm taking care of myself.

00:47:04.720 --> 00:47:06.320
- Yeah. Thank you.

00:47:06.320 --> 00:47:08.020
There are four of you who would...

00:47:09.840 --> 00:47:10.673
Yes.

00:47:16.490 --> 00:47:19.873
- [Audience Member] Hi, thank
you so much for sharing.

00:47:21.810 --> 00:47:26.023
How did, you mentioned God
